### Output configuration
#
# Geometry (mode/position) MUST be declared here, not only in a profile
# tool: every `swaymsg reload` re-applies sway's stored output configs and
# any output without an explicit mode/position is forced to its preferred
# mode and auto-arranged (black flash + monitors jumping). Declaring the
# same values sway would otherwise keep makes reload a no-op.
#
# Matching is by name first, then by IDENTIFIER ("make model serial", see
# `swaymsg -t get_outputs`). ORDER MATTERS (sway quirk): a name-based block
# stored after an identifier block RESETS the identifier block's fields
# (supersede_output_config in sway/config/output.c). So name blocks must
# come FIRST, identifier blocks LAST — the identifier then wins the merge.
#
# You can get the names and identifiers of your outputs by running:
# swaymsg -t get_outputs
# Read `man 5 sway-output` for more information about this section.

output * bg ../wallpaper.jpg fill

# tecnalia (laptop) — name-based blocks: only apply when those outputs
# connect, so docked/undocked both work. Assumed docked arrangement
# (eDP-1 builtin left, two externals to the right); verify the real port
# names on the machine and adjust. Mode is only set where a specific
# refresh is wanted — unset = preferred. KEEP BEFORE the identifier blocks.
output eDP-1 {
    position 0,0
}

output HDMI-A-1 {
    mode 1920x1080@60Hz
    position 1920,0
}

output DP-1 {
    mode 1920x1080@60Hz
    position 3840,0
}

# mithrandir — identifier blocks (override the name blocks above; the
# identifier follows the physical monitor, so this stays machine-agnostic).
# AOC 24G2W1G4 (DP-1), right monitor
output "AOC 24G2W1G4 0x0000C31B" {
    mode 1920x1080@144Hz
    position 1920,0
}

# Samsung S24F350 (HDMI-A-1), left monitor
output "Samsung Electric Company S24F350 H4ZH401731" {
    mode 1920x1080@60Hz
    position 0,0
}
